    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fc059fa1-3a39-5276-a25a-99cdbc4f0cfd",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and $2$nd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
