      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}.\n$$",
